01:01:30,000 --> 01:01:36,000
Eurovision Song Contest: The Story of Fire Saga is a 2020 American musical romantic comedy film directed by David Dobkin, written by Will Ferrell and Harper Steele, and starring
Ferrell, Rachel McAdams, Dan Stevens, Melissanthi Mahut, Mikael Persbrandt, Ólafur Darri Ólafsson, Graham Norton, Demi Lovato, Pierce Brosnan, and Elín Petersdóttir.

11
01:07:39,000 --> 01:07:45,000
It follows the personally close Icelandic singers Lars Erickssong (Ferrell) and Sigrit Ericksdóttir
(McAdams) as they are given the chance to represent their country in the Eurovision Song Contest.

12
01:13:48,000 --> 01:13:54,000
Development of a film based on the Eurovision Song Contest began in 2018, with Ferrell, a self-described
follower of the event, attending the 2018 and 2019 editions to conceive the characters and story.

13
01:19:57,000 --> 01:20:03,000
The film was officially announced in June 2018, and filming took place
between August and October 2019 in Scotland, Iceland, and England.

14
01:26:06,000 --> 01:26:12,000
The Story of Fire Saga was originally scheduled for a May 2020 release on
Netflix to coincide with the Eurovision Song Contest 2020.

15
01:32:15,000 --> 01:32:21,000
Due to the COVID-19 pandemic, the 2020 contest was canceled, and the
film was subsequently released a month later, on June 26.

16
01:38:24,000 --> 01:38:30,000
It received mixed reviews from critics, who praised the original
music but criticised the screenplay and runtime.

17
01:44:33,000 --> 01:44:39,000
The film received a nomination for Best Original Song at
the 93rd Academy Awards (for "Husavik").

18
01:50:42,000 --> 01:50:48,000
The film explores themes of pop star, competition,
rivalry, aspiring singer, singing competition.

19
01:56:51,000 --> 01:56:57,000
The tone is lighthearted.
